 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Tool Manipulation — Innate Technique (3rd level)</em></p><p>At 3rd level, when you imbue a tool, you can spend an additional 2 CE to create a <em>Floating Tool</em>. You can command a <em>Floating Tool</em> as an action to hover up to 35 feet in any direction and make a melee attack using your CE modifier. The <em>Floating Tool</em> deals its normal weapon damage or 1d4 bludgeoning, slashing, or piercing if it is an improvised weapon. You can only have one floating tool at a time and it falls to the ground if it is more than 120 ft from you.</p>\n<p>A <em>Floating Tool</em> has AC equal to your CE save DC and hit points equal to 5 x your proficiency bonus + 10 for each grade above 4th if it is a cursed tool. A <em>Floating Tool</em> reduced to 0 HP is destroyed unless it is a cursed tool, in which case it loses the benefits of <em>Floating Tool</em>. You can spend 2 CE as a bonus action to return the effect of <em>Floating Tool</em> to the cursed tool by touching it.  </p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
